# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# What this repo is for: the NetHack 5.0.0 -> Vulture SDL2 port and the tooling
# that builds it. Everything ignored below is either (a) somebody else's git
# repo, (b) regenerable output, or (c) a large binary that adds no history.
#
# Note: vulture5-win/.gitignore is upstream NetHack's and still applies on top
# of this file - it already covers *.o, *.a, tags, editor backups and so on.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# (a) Nested git repos - upstream sources and the pinned 3.6.6 baseline.
#     These are checkouts of other people's history; tracking them here would
#     embed them as broken pseudo-submodules.
/refs/
/vulture-baseline/
/win-build/

# (b) Regenerable output.
#     VultureNetHack/ is the shipped package: toolchain/finalize_exe.sh builds
#     the exe into it, and its config/ + tiles/ are deployed copies of
#     vulture5-win/win/vulture/gamedata/, which IS tracked. Nothing original
#     lives here - but see the note in IMPLEMENTATION_LOG.md, because the two
#     tile trees are currently maintained in parallel by hand.
/VultureNetHack/
/vulture5-win/binary/
/vulture5-win/win/vulture/build_nethack_3_6_0/

# (c) Large binaries with no reason to be in history.
/toolchain/msys2-installer.exe
/hearse/
/shots/

# Build artefacts not already covered by the upstream ignore file.
*.exe
*.dll
*.res
*.stackdump
/vulture5-win/src/GNUmakefile

# NOTE - a previous version of this file listed the player's runtime-state
# filenames here (vulture.conf, livelog, record, bon[A-Z]*, ...) "for
# safety".  That was a mistake that cost real files: git on Windows matches
# ignore patterns CASE-INSENSITIVELY (core.ignorecase=true), so bon[A-Z]*
# matched src/boneS.c, and the unanchored names matched legitimate tracked
# paths like win/vulture/gamedata/config/vulture.conf - both were silently
# excluded from the initial commit and were only recoverable because a copy
# of the tree survived inside WSL.  The player's real runtime state lives
# OUTSIDE this repo (ProgramData / AppData) or inside /VultureNetHack/,
# which is already ignored as a whole - so no per-filename rules are needed,
# and none should ever be re-added.
*.bak
*.prezoom
